=== P3 Dashboard widget 0006 AutomationHistoryWidget (Android) ===
Capability: Jetpack Compose + Material 3, Kotlin 2.2.x — AVAILABLE (JDK 21, Android SDK, gradlew).
P3 core prerequisites DONE: A1 theme/tokens, A3 nav, A5 data-layer/viewmodels, A6 live, A8/A0 scaffold.

Documented deviations (Honesty Covenant #9 — no silent drift):
 1. Gradle module is ':android' (settings.gradle.kts: projectDir=app). Prompt gate says ':app:' which
    does not exist in this build; the settings file documents the skew ("every P3/A* prompt gate
    addresses ':android:'"). Gate below uses ':android:'.
 2. Build prerequisite restored: the shared KMP client (io.teslasync.shared.core.api.generated.*) is a
    gitignored OpenAPI artifact (.gitignore 'apps/**/generated/'); absent in a fresh worktree, which
    broke ':shared:core' compilation (and thus the whole app) at HEAD. Regenerated reproducibly via the
    committed P1/S2 pipeline 'apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ps1' from the committed spec
    'api/openapi/teslasync.openapi.json' (GEN wrote 10 Kotlin + 10 C# models). No shared-core logic edited.
 3. Production files live in the mandated surface dir com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/AutomationHistoryWidget/
    but declare package io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.automationhistory — a valid Kotlin package
    cannot contain a hyphen or PascalCase segment, so detekt InvalidPackageDeclaration is file-suppressed
    with justification. Mirrors the Windows P2 analog, which models the surface as a directory.
 4. Tests live in the standard src/test + src/androidTest source sets, scoped to this surface (same as the
    Windows P2 analog's separate test project). The offline gate runs JVM unit tests; the Compose UI/a11y
    tests are instrumented (connectedAndroidTest, device-only) — authored + compile-verified here.
 5. Host wiring (registering the AutomationsStore in DataContainer + grid placement) is outside allowed
    files; the widget binds to the shared S7/S8 Automations feed via an injected source (host-ready).
